# Core design principle: AI as an agent, not a chatbox

A simple AI chat mode is useful, but the product you’re describing needs an **agentic workflow**.

That means the AI needs structured abilities:

```plain text
User request
  ↓
AI interprets task
  ↓
AI creates plan
  ↓
User approves plan
  ↓
AI executes command
  ↓
Terminal returns output
  ↓
AI assesses output
  ↓
AI continues / stops / asks for approval
  ↓
Final summary
```


This is different from a plain chatbot because the AI can actually operate on the Linux system.

