# Command risk model

You should classify AI-proposed commands before execution.

## Safe read-only commands

Can optionally run with minimal confirmation:

```shell script
pwd
ls
cat
head
tail
df -h
free -h
uname -a
whoami
id
ps aux
systemctl status service
journalctl -xe --no-pager
git status
```


## Medium-risk commands

Require confirmation:

```shell script
mkdir
touch
cp
mv
chmod
chown
pip install
npm install
git checkout
git pull
systemctl restart
```


## High-risk commands

Require explicit confirmation and maybe typed approval:

```shell script
rm
rm -rf
dd
mkfs
fdisk
parted
mount
umount
sudo
apt install
dnf install
pacman -S
systemctl stop
systemctl disable
iptables
ufw
curl | sh
wget | sh
chmod -R
chown -R
```


## Forbidden or strongly blocked by default

Should require settings override:

```shell script
rm -rf /
rm -rf /*
:(){ :|:& };:
dd if=/dev/zero of=/dev/sda
mkfs.ext4 /dev/sda
chmod -R 777 /
chown -R user:user /
```


