# AI workflow modes

ZetaTerminal could support several levels of autonomy.

## Mode 1 — Ask only

AI answers questions but does not execute commands.

Example:

```plain text
How do I check why nginx is failing?
```


AI responds with explanation and suggested commands.

---

## Mode 2 — Plan only

AI creates a step-by-step plan but does not run it.

Example:

```plain text
Diagnose why my disk is full.
```


AI returns:

```plain text
1. Run df -h
2. Run du -h --max-depth=1 ~
3. Check journal size
4. Suggest cleanup
```


---

## Mode 3 — Confirm each command

AI proposes each command, user approves one at a time.

This should be the default for early versions.

---

## Mode 4 — Auto-run safe commands

AI can automatically run read-only diagnostic commands, but asks before changing anything.

Example:

```shell script
df -h
lsblk
systemctl status docker
journalctl -u docker --no-pager -n 100
```


---

## Mode 5 — Agent mode

AI can run multiple commands in a loop, but still stops for dangerous operations.

This is the advanced version.

---

# Recommended default

For initial releases:

```plain text
Default AI mode: Confirm each command
Auto-run allowed: Read-only diagnostics only
Destructive commands: Always require explicit approval
sudo commands: Always require explicit approval
```


This balances usefulness with safety.

