# Important architectural decision: visible terminal vs hidden executor

You have two possible execution strategies.

---

## Option A — Execute AI commands in the visible terminal

Pros:

- Fully transparent
- User sees everything
- Feels natural
- Easy to audit

Cons:

- Harder to reliably capture command completion/output
- Interactive commands can complicate automation
- User typing can interfere with agent execution

---

## Option B — Execute AI commands in a separate controlled backend shell

Pros:

- Easier to capture stdout/stderr/exit code
- Better for agent loops
- Safer separation from user terminal
- Easier to parse results

Cons:

- Less transparent unless mirrored to UI
- Environment may differ from visible terminal
- Interactive commands are harder

---

## Recommended approach

Use both:

```plain text
Visible terminal:
- Normal user work
- Interactive commands
- Manual execution

AI executor:
- Non-interactive diagnostic and remediation commands
- Captured output
- Agent loop
```


The AI executor should mirror commands and output into an **AI execution log**, so nothing is hidden.

For commands that require interactivity, the AI should hand off to the visible terminal.

Example:

```plain text
This step requires interactive input. I can paste the command into the terminal for you, but you should run it manually.
```


